  "claim_scope": "Candidate C4c: the bounded ESSO model (two lanes, one domain, two claimants, eight atoms per cell) is an inductive two-solver contract for the certificate relation with eight invariants including the derived normative partition and same-domain backing, eight named mutants each attributed to one invariant, and a runtime link to the Python checker. Candidate C4b: the bounded Lean model (three lanes, two domains, two claimants over natural numbers) derives the normative partition, same-domain backing, open-terminal coverage, the exact current-profile custody special case, and the registered-empty-only consequence of having no receipt-backed producer, and refutes reserve masking, unassigned atoms, producer-less enabled lanes, and over-entitled terminal claims; bound by its own compile/axioms/pin gate and by the O-008 packet as a second Lean subject. Candidate C4a: GlobalAccountingAllocationCertificateV1, the state-keyed sidecar checker over the control-domain vocabulary (claimant entitlements, unencumbered reserves, pending external obligations, terminal bindings) with a producer registry exhaustive over the twelve lanes (EXTERNAL_CUSTODY registered-empty-disabled, PROOF_REWARDS registered-empty-blocked, ten NO_PRODUCER lanes blocked on their unresolved policies), fourteen closed reject codes in fixed check precedence, checked u128 folds, derived field-ownership/terminal-binding/allocation roots, and a Python/Rust twin replaying one rendered twenty-five-vector golden fixture (three accepts: registered-empty over empty state, acknowledged outbox, drained terminal; one reject per reachable code; root-pinning synthetic fragments). Research-only: no lane producer is receipt-backed, nothing is mounted, and the reject-is-no-op contract is asserted on state roots.",
